## Model card

- OpenCode Zen alias `opencode/big-pickle`, officially a stealth model with temporary free access. Underlying developer, checkpoint, architecture, parameter count, license, cutoff and exact release are undisclosed. [Service documentation](https://opencode.ai/docs/zen/).
- Chat-completions endpoint supports coding-agent use; independently verified context/output limits and full modality specification were not established.

### Raw benchmarks found

An independent evaluator reports SWE Atlas Codebase QnA 63/124 = 50.81%, run August 11, 2026, mini-swe-agent 2.4.6 and Harbor 0.18.0. One trial rather than official three, reduced compute, two tasks with unscored rubrics; strict treatment 61/124 = 49.2%. Scale did not verify the run. This is a dated alias snapshot, not proof of current checkpoint performance. [Evaluator and logs](https://github.com/PhillipChaffee/big-pickle-swe-atlas). GPQA, HLE, current exact-checkpoint SWE Verified and long-context retrieval: no verified public score found.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Excluded from aggregation: the historical coding benchmark is real evidence but does not identify the current stealth checkpoint or establish enough dimensions for a defensible Overall score. No scores borrowed from rumored DeepSeek or GLM identities.

